WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:02.719
Cleo sighed.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.265
Did law officers ever get to relax?

3
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:09.425
Roscoe got up from his desk.

4
00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:13.039
"I'm going to ask your new friends a few questions."

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.521
"Violet and Sasha?" Cleo asked.

6
00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:18.239
"That's ridiculous.

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.740
They aren't thieves.

8
00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:22.116
I should know!"

9
00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:25.402
"We'll see."

10
00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:27.871
Roscoe went outside.

11
00:00:27.872 --> 00:00:32.058
Cleo followed him.

12
00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:36.719
They walked into the lobby of the boardinghouse.

13
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.780
"Afternoon, Mrs. Chatsworth," Roscoe said to the owner.

14
00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:42.914
"Two cats checked in this morning.

15
00:00:42.915 --> 00:00:44.677
Are they still around?"

16
00:00:44.678 --> 00:00:47.334
Mrs. Chatsworth shook her head.

17
00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:49.773
"They picked up their trunk and left.

18
00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:52.552
They didn't even look at their room."

19
00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:56.483
"Did you see which way they went?" Cleo asked.

20
00:00:56.484 --> 00:00:58.672
Mrs. Chatsworth nodded.

21
00:00:58.673 --> 00:01:01.632
"They were headed for the hills."

22
00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:06.948
"Thank you, ma'am," Roscoe said.

23
00:01:06.949 --> 00:01:11.626
Before long Roscoe and Cleo were up in the hills.

24
00:01:11.627 --> 00:01:15.347
They searched everywhere.

25
00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:18.179
Cleo wiped sweat from her brow.

26
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.024
"You know, lots of folks got off the train together.

27
00:01:22.025 --> 00:01:24.426
Any of them could be the thieves."

28
00:01:24.427 --> 00:01:27.337
Roscoe raised an eyebrow.

29
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:30.847
"Sasha and Violet brought that heavy trunk up here.

30
00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:33.088
Don't you think that's strange?"

31
00:01:33.089 --> 00:01:36.519
Cleo shrugged. "It's strange.

32
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.110
But it doesn't make them thieves."

33
00:01:39.111 --> 00:01:45.985
Just then they heard a rustle in some tall grass.

34
00:01:45.986 --> 00:01:48.625
Roscoe held a finger to his lips.

35
00:01:48.626 --> 00:01:55.139
Cleo nodded. They crept closer.

36
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.575
Roscoe moved the grass out of the way. "Zeke!"

37
00:01:58.576 --> 00:02:01.948
The toad seemed to be looking for something.

38
00:02:01.949 --> 00:02:05.703
"I'm glad I bumped into you two," Zeke said.

39
00:02:05.704 --> 00:02:08.716
"Someone stole my shovel!"

40
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:11.599
Roscoe gave Cleo a look.

41
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.768
"I think we know who stole it."

42
00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:16.062
She rolled her eyes.

43
00:02:16.063 --> 00:02:21.679
"Sasha and Violet aren't thieves!" She turned back to Zeke.

44
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.670
"If we find your shovel, we'll let you know."

45
00:02:24.671 --> 00:02:32.297
"Thanks." Zeke walked toward the riverbed.

46
00:02:32.298 --> 00:02:36.318
Roscoe and Cleo walked farther.

47
00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:40.669
Then Cleo saw something sticking out of the dirt.

48
00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.917
"Zeke's shovel!" She ran over and grabbed it.

49
00:02:44.918 --> 00:02:47.324
"My friends didn't steal it.

50
00:02:47.325 --> 00:02:50.491
It looks like Zeke just misplaced it!"

51
00:02:50.492 --> 00:02:53.301
Roscoe's ears pricked up.

52
00:02:53.302 --> 00:02:58.407
"I hear voices." He started walking down a trail.

53
00:02:58.408 --> 00:03:01.073
Cleo followed Roscoe.

54
00:03:01.074 --> 00:03:06.803
They soon spotted Violet and Sasha walking toward town.

55
00:03:06.804 --> 00:03:11.137
The cats stopped when they noticed the two law officers.

56
00:03:11.138 --> 00:03:17.589
"Oh, howdy, Cleo," Sasha said. "Hello, Sheriff."

57
00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:22.085
"What are you two doing out here?" Cleo asked.

58
00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:24.648
"Us?" Violet asked.

59
00:03:24.649 --> 00:03:29.643
"We're . . . um, enjoying the scenery."

60
00:03:29.644 --> 00:03:32.175
"Yep!" Sasha said quickly.

61
00:03:32.176 --> 00:03:36.045
"We're just taking a walk!"

62
00:03:36.046 --> 00:03:39.898
Cleo noticed the cats looked nervous.

63
00:03:39.899 --> 00:03:43.579
And both had dirt on their dresses.

64
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.003
This was mighty suspicious!

65
00:03:47.004 --> 00:03:49.250
Cleo narrowed her eyes.

66
00:03:49.251 --> 00:03:57.922
"Where's that trunk you two were carrying?"

